{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "db54940f-4d80-8869-912c-c55f6ea83361",
  "created_at": "2026-02-05T10:49:49-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Lidia Fortes",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Anita Chaudhry",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:47:55-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Anita. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:47:59-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, hi, good morning. Um, I'm not sure I've got the right department. My fence came down in the wind, and I'm trying to figure out who I'd talk to about it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:48:09-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Came down how, did the whole thing fall over, or just a section?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:48:14-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Most of it. A good run of it is flat in the yard, and some of it went over into the lot beside me. Sorry, hold on, I'm stretching this phone cord across the kitchen so I can see out the window."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:48:27-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No worries, take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:48:29-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So there's boards and posts and wire all over. I guess what I'm asking is, does the city come and clear that kind of thing? Or is that on me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:48:39-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. So, is the debris on your own property, or is any of it in the street or on a sidewalk?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:48:46-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Mostly mine. Some went in the neighbor's yard, but nothing's out in the road. Wait, is that the difference? I thought a mess was a mess."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:48:54-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It can matter. If it's in the public way, that's Public Services. If it's on private property, generally the property owner handles it, though they might pick up regular trash if it's bundled properly. I'd call Public Services to confirm what they'll take."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:49:07-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Services. And that's not you folks?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:49:10-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not for cleanup, no. We deal with permits and inspections. If there were a safety problem with a structure, we'd come into it, but loose boards in a yard is theirs."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:49:20-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so I was close. Not you, but them. Do you have a number, or do I just ask for them at City Hall?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:49:28-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ask for Public Services at the main City Hall line, they'll connect you. Do you want me to transfer you now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:49:35-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, would you? That'd be easier. I'd probably write the wrong thing down. [pause] And just so I've got it, they're the ones for the boards, not the, the inspection people."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:49:44-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. Hold on one moment, I'll put you through."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T10:49:47-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, dear."
    }
  ],
